{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact b765e6bd7902c0042baf1c6ec98c9a85e6d02215, all 39 changed paths versus main 8becbb0, S4 results note first. Reviewed in a separate detached checkout: npm ci, npm ci --prefix experiments/pds, npm run check (0), npm run test:flows -- --group participation (18/18: six host scenarios, ten browser and CLI scenarios, two parents), npm test (242/242, 0 skipped); tree clean afterwards. All 80 sourceHashes in experiments/host-flows.json and all 80 in experiments/participation.json match HEAD; case names and counts match the test files; no credentials, tokens or private keys appear in the retained evidence, docs or note; src/ carries no demo-domain vocabulary and no innerHTML, eval, Function or dynamic import. The two screenshots show the shell in the exact state the gate produces at its screenshot step.\n\nVerified in code. The origin and signing boundaries hold: the service refuses any Host or Origin other than its own and emits no cross-origin headers; the browser signs on the main thread and the worker is sent only source, invitation, verified inputs, intents, action names, payloads and query parameters; the CLI identity file is created once at 0600 and only its public key travels; the host verifies every intent signature before append and signs only entries with the genesis sequencer key, and preview folds sign nothing. Publication recovery: account credentials, source, writer key and the request CID are persisted before any network I/O, a lost provisioning reply reconciles only against the exact anchor, an existing genesis with another CID refuses, the browser freezes source, grants and creation ID before calling create and refuses later draft edits, and the CLI create retry returns the identical result while a changed grant refuses with creation_conflict. Exact retry bytes: the browser resends the stored block, the CLI re-verifies the retained file against the current anchor and its recorded work before resending, and the sequencer retry index returns the original receipt; the CLI test pins byte-identical file contents and the same position across a retry. Head and frontier coherence: host reads are serialized per app, submit reports the larger of the folder and sequencer heads with the folder frontier, and the folder refuses rollback and fork. Form refresh preservation: one editor node is reused across redraws and the transport-refusal test types into the form, refreshes, then saves from the preserved form. The worker verifies the complete signed prefix before folding and refuses a host response that differs from the pinned invitation; only worker-verified inputs enter the device cache. Hostile views: text is built with DOM text APIs only, the Inlay allow-list admits Panel, Text and Action with children, action and label, an unsupported auto-submit property renders as unavailable with zero signatures and zero entries, and the CSP restricts scripts and workers to the shell origin.\n\nNon-blocking observations for S5 or S6, none changing a condition of satisfaction. Sample actions in the draft preview, the verified-input cache restore path, and the pending preview card are implemented but have no pinning test; the \"Try sample action\" locator count at participation.test.ts line 41 is a statement, not an assertion. The external-resource assertion is trivially satisfied because the hostile string lands as a text node; the real guard is the primitive allow-list, and the signatures counter has no positive control showing it increments on a real Save. flush resends already-recorded intents on every retry, relying on the retry index; skipping recorded entries would be simpler. flush and reconcile both use set rather than update on the same outbox key, so a reconcile can be overwritten until the next refresh. A 4xx from create is presented as \"could not be confirmed\" rather than as a refusal. The host query method returns 503 for malformed params JSON where 400 fits. The retained S3 evidence files now hash-mismatch HEAD on testdata/apps/fixtures.ts and package.json after this head's fixture and script edits; the S6 acceptance run refreshes them. Several guards are confirmed by probe only: the Host and Origin gate, static path containment, the creation-ID regex, the 100-waiting cap, the CLI mode, symlink, closure and outside-source refusals, and the worker invitation mismatch.\n\nArchitecture: host service and client layers (architecture sections 5 and 7) with the runtime and protocol contracts unchanged; the engine and application profile CIDs are untouched at this head; the source contract's open-object wording adopts the S3 observation. Security: signing keys stay on the client, the host never signs for an actor, local secrets are owner-only files, untrusted view content cannot execute, fetch or sign, and every uncertain reply is retained rather than invented; no unresolved defect. Simplification: skip recorded entries in flush and use update for outbox transitions; neither weakens the gate. Nothing here adopts the plan-review recommendations.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:9c03f4d7554009d0e932e9f6620af2cf79418b3e","head":"b765e6bd7902c0042baf1c6ec98c9a85e6d02215","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:2eb6a26065dc929b270bba62041cdc2d2ba8ff2f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:2eb6a26065dc929b270bba62041cdc2d2ba8ff2f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}